{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"continuous-prominent-zander","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe first proposal mixed forward validity with historical convention. Revise it to a small deterministic floor intended to have no false positives, then use accepted history only as an adversarial counterexample corpus.\n\n## Approach\nTest failure patterns rather than preferred prose style. A rule qualifies for the floor only when the detected state is structurally incompatible with an executable plan; otherwise it remains advisory. Search closed tickets carrying signed plan-review and completion evidence, inspect every matching candidate in context, and narrow or remove any rule with a legitimate match.\n\n## Criteria Under Review\n1. An Acceptance Criteria checkbox must contain non-whitespace text after the checkbox marker.\n2. Two Acceptance Criteria items must not be exact duplicates after joining continuations and normalizing whitespace/case.\n3. Active execution prose must not contain a bare unresolved sentinel (`TBD`, `TODO`, `FIXME`, or `???`) in Approach, Scope, Testing, or Acceptance Criteria; ignore fenced code, inline code, quotations, examples, explicit removal/prohibition assertions, and superseded/history sections.\n4. Structured file-impact entries, when present, must have a nonempty path and nonempty reason; absence of file impact is allowed.\n5. A `[rebar:<id>]` prerequisite citation used as plan evidence must resolve to a direct verified upstream dependency; ignore literal examples in code spans/fences.\n\n## Scope\nRead-only ticket-store analysis. The only mutation is the final findings comment on this ticket; no repository files or other ticket material will be changed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every criterion under review has a documented historical search and cited matching tickets, verified by the final findings comment.\n- [ ] Every legitimate matching ticket is treated as a counterexample and causes the rule to be narrowed or rejected, verified by before/after detection wording in the final findings.\n- [ ] The final recommendation clearly separates hard-floor rules from advisory signals, verified by a structured classification table in the final findings.\n- [ ] If a rule has no historical match, the finding says that explicitly without claiming proof of soundness, verified by the final findings comment.","id":"e759-c562-e233-4108","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["analysis","clarity","plan-review"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Adversarially validate a revised deterministic clarity floor"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785190840702646001,"uuid":"ca2468de-52c5-4208-84f7-d657e2bb8808"}